{"id":"249609e07ffaed64","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-prop-filter.md","title":"Filter Properties","display":"prop-filter — Filter Properties","type":"proposition","metadata":{"type":"proposition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-prop-filter","aliases":["58-prop-filter"],"display":"prop-filter — Filter Properties","depends_on":["[[../batch15/58-df-filter.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"proposition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-prop-filter"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-prop-filter</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"prop-filter — Filter Properties"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"1331244a5201bb99\" href=\"?note=1331244a5201bb99\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-filter.md\">../batch15/58-df-filter.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F,X\\in V\">\\(F,X\\in V\\)</span> (candidate family and carrier set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\subseteq_X\\coloneqq\\subseteq\\cap(\\mathcal P(X)\\times\\mathcal P(X))\">\\(\\subseteq_X\\coloneqq\\subseteq\\cap(\\mathcal P(X)\\times\\mathcal P(X))\\)</span> (inclusion order)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Filter}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Filter}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (order-theoretic filter predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"1331244a5201bb99\" href=\"?note=1331244a5201bb99\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-filter.md\">../batch15/58-df-filter.md</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}filter}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Filter}_S(F,\\mathcal P(X),\\subseteq_X)\\land\\emptyset\\notin F\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;F\\subseteq\\mathcal P(X)\\land X\\in F\\land\\emptyset\\notin F\n\\land\\forall A,B\\in F\\;(A\\cap B\\in F)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A\\in F\\;\\forall B\\in\\mathcal P(X)\\;(A\\subseteq B\\to B\\in F).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}filter}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Filter}_S(F,\\mathcal P(X),\\subseteq_X)\\land\\emptyset\\notin F\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;F\\subseteq\\mathcal P(X)\\land X\\in F\\land\\emptyset\\notin F\n\\land\\forall A,B\\in F\\;(A\\cap B\\in F)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A\\in F\\;\\forall B\\in\\mathcal P(X)\\;(A\\subseteq B\\to B\\in F).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The left side specializes the book's order-theoretic filter predicate to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(\\mathcal P(X),\\subseteq_X)\">\\((\\mathcal P(X),\\subseteq_X)\\)</span> and then imposes properness.</li>\n<li>Without <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\\notin F\">\\(\\emptyset\\notin F\\)</span>, the order-theoretic predicate also admits the improper filter <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P(X)\">\\(\\mathcal P(X)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Every quantifier on the elementary side is set-bounded; in particular, supersets are selected from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal P(X)\">\\(\\mathcal P(X)\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch15/58-df-filter.md","status":"resolved","id":"1331244a5201bb99","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-filter.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-filter.md","status":"resolved","id":"1331244a5201bb99","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Filter}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (order-theoretic filter predicate, see [[../batch15/58-df-filter.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"F,X\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\subseteq_X\\coloneqq\\subseteq\\cap(\\mathcal P(X)\\times\\mathcal P(X))","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Filter}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}filter}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{Filter}_S(F,\\mathcal P(X),\\subseteq_X)\\land\\emptyset\\notin F\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&F\\subseteq\\mathcal P(X)\\land X\\in F\\land\\emptyset\\notin F\n\\land\\forall A,B\\in F\\;(A\\cap B\\in F)\\\\\n&\\land\\forall A\\in F\\;\\forall B\\in\\mathcal P(X)\\;(A\\subseteq B\\to B\\in F).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"(\\mathcal P(X),\\subseteq_X)","display":false},{"tex":"\\emptyset\\notin F","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal P(X)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal P(X)","display":false}],"bytes":1255,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-3957","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-prop-filter.md|58-prop-filter]]（batch03）"}],"outgoing":["1331244a5201bb99"]}